.TH std::unordered_multiset::size 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::unordered_multiset::size \- std::unordered_multiset::size

.SH Synopsis
size_type size() const noexcept;  \fI(since C++11)\fP

Returns the number of elements in the container, i.e. std::distance(begin(), end()).

.SH Parameters

\fI(none)\fP

.SH Return value

The number of elements in the container.

.SH Complexity

Constant.

.SH Example


// Run this code

#include <cassert>
#include <unordered_set>

int main()
{
    std::unordered_multiset<int> nums{4, 2, 4, 2};
    assert(nums.size() == 4);
}

